# Evaluation Engine — Function Rationale & References

This document explains **why each metric function was chosen**, which standard it maps to, how the scoring logic was derived, and what academic or industry sources support it. It is the companion to the four Python files in `evaluator/`.

>** Every function in the evaluation engine is grounded in a published standard or peer-reviewed usability research. The functions are structural proxies — not direct measurements — because the system evaluates static HTML without rendering. This limitation is acknowledged explicitly in each module's header.

