## Why These Three Standards?

These three were chosen because together they cover the full usability and accessibility evaluation space from three complementary perspectives:

| Standard | Perspective | Evaluation method |
|---|---|---|
| ISO 9241-11:2018 | Task-performance (empirical usability) | Structural proxies for effectiveness, efficiency, satisfaction |
| Nielsen (1994) | Expert heuristic review | Structural proxies for 8 of 10 heuristics |
| WCAG 2.2 (W3C, 2023) | Technical accessibility compliance | Automated rule checking + structural proxies |

They are also the three most widely cited frameworks in academic HCI literature and are used in professional usability audits. Using all three provides triangulation — a weakness identified by two or more frameworks is more reliably a real problem.

